 "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241604} {:answer/id #uuid "78aac119-4dde-5951-ad35-559a566ff943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242243} {:answer/id #uuid "a223bb82-bec3-501b-aded-253a53009b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242600} {:answer/id #uuid "c3968252-fc1a-5b53-9617-261d78f533e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a223bb82-bec3-501b-aded-253a53009b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242600} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf01c73d-57cf-5598-8656-0c2a923068f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c5d0d5a-1c35-5e42-acae-01a474314ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-1087" :question/problem "Calculate $det(T)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10-17\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-17 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455009c1-cd1b-5980-bebc-005c166aaab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{243}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248047} {:answer/id #uuid "896f555a-8df1-54e2-8351-8c2d255e5f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248645} {:answer/id #uuid "af350e46-2ecb-56b8-977a-f33f11df9722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248994} {:answer/id #uuid "c7fb154d-0bb2-50c5-a991-8b8bf26ab955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249203} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b780a7-5d64-5db2-a401-0d776743ab54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "896f555a-8df1-54e2-8351-8c2d255e5f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248645} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c672aeb-3770-5ff7-9ee1-eb36a7e65af5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8ba6724-aa4a-53a8-8ea0-e040d768a286" :question/math-academy-id "q-113989" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3(-1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{3(-3)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{81}) \\\\  & =-\\left(-\\frac{26}{81}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "147b8607-00ab-583f-9d29-c36db3ffb93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247609} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9923c0-68fb-5db2-a270-b22a0a565a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{(5x+10)}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248673} {:answer/id #uuid "b955e3b8-b464-5b10-97ae-eea2d8b024ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249080} {:answer/id #uuid "efb057ba-bc50-5a4b-9c8c-026e21fb0356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249528} {:answer/id #uuid "f825b128-d786-54b0-9c93-577427b75d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "147b8607-00ab-583f-9d29-c36db3ffb93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247609} :answer-field/id #uuid "1beb6b75-3505-5fda-ac7d-3d7a94737480" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249718}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "421599a5-1cf3-595e-9d3b-cce9b649fa80" :question/math-academy-id "q-11410" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)={(5x+10)}^{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{6},\\,g=5x+10\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6{g}^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =6{g}^{5}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =30(5x+10{)}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b409ba-367b-57b5-9cc8-a4cc43e79abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250629} {:answer/id #uuid "111ce74d-7bba-5493-aa71-8ee83c614b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250701} {:answer/id #uuid "47fa1918-9d0b-56af-8644-cc0f2fc9b075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251150} {:answer/id #uuid "59b9af1c-53b9-5140-bb46-d0e5ad2ee18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251290} {:answer/id #uuid "ee44218a-1840-5afa-8d45-0c6d89d6e523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59b9af1c-53b9-5140-bb46-d0e5ad2ee18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251290} :answer-field/id #uuid "93a5d72e-dcdb-5c71-8e9e-3a86d0045b79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b53c0c18-d59e-56b1-837f-3b6d41491a5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-11646" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(L)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle L=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(L) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =12-(-10) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0209a06e-c872-52c8-83aa-6e78fe082784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250573} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8f8e5e-07ec-513d-8935-253e50a8994b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250679} {:answer/id #uuid "5c767359-7b77-5594-a325-0a9b4ca901af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251315} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8e6d11-24ab-54f4-9302-a197b45ae78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} {:answer/id #uuid "e407a6b3-d6da-578c-aa7b-c0b520a0af0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd8e6d11-24ab-54f4-9302-a197b45ae78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5bd1bd-eab3-5250-8633-db4827abfabb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "605f5d22-0a36-54b2-9fda-393ada9a651b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11653" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(M)=2$, what is the value of $w?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d17cada-80e5-58f6-aeed-2e93b5243081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250667} {:answer/id #uuid "2afc783b-b9ed-5bd3-afa0-161d31d4cab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250919} {:answer/id #uuid "5611e50e-f57e-53b9-ad85-570dd238b4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251258} {:answer/id #uuid "6848ae3e-4124-5b9d-b387-6eb18ca003db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251408} {:answer/id #uuid "748c5c61-72ec-5a32-94cf-d53bf7b85eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2afc783b-b9ed-5bd3-afa0-161d31d4cab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250919} :answer-field/id #uuid "174407a9-f46d-55da-8697-5dbc5ce40bfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6494dcea-ff4c-57dc-b8ab-235d70e87dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-119361" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +1+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1+({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253571 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1666eb4d-d4a7-5e6b-9ab8-611863630400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250744} {:answer/id #uuid "671b51fc-531d-5b84-807b-36d54aed2521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251399} {:answer/id #uuid "8919a4b0-5234-55e6-83d8-2a41e35d8daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+{cos}^{3}⁡\\