orname{cos}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1815e8ee-c289-5f64-9f4d-5df43b4aab39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250764} {:answer/id #uuid "25423e87-2e31-52ea-9bed-9680a8ad4d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250872} {:answer/id #uuid "380b2f49-3850-505e-a125-48611fc7669a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251019} {:answer/id #uuid "b6fc9b1c-0a28-54c2-82c9-b8ff1ad7eae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252166} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0ddaa2-dc14-5f83-8293-f70b43e52381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "380b2f49-3850-505e-a125-48611fc7669a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251019} :answer-field/id #uuid "a308e80e-fc90-57c9-9815-5d63c4e60f59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e264613-6b71-5c6c-b1c0-6da9257b1f1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119371" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e29407f-0306-5cd7-ab50-d46e971435f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251071} {:answer/id #uuid "6218e58c-9107-5231-b02a-3a84de60083e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251349} {:answer/id #uuid "ae27a1dd-2895-5936-945a-8057f5eb72ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} {:answer/id #uuid "d57697f1-9470-5638-87e8-1592607aa161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252444} {:answer/id #uuid "f07f9d80-b3ae-5297-8430-2159434cec87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae27a1dd-2895-5936-945a-8057f5eb72ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad77e15e-6b7f-5b66-be54-92af8304ca70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f206d2c2-ee8e-56e4-8de0-ea23491335cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119379" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0decdc0f-4b98-5c65-a3b0-d86ae94d22ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250673} {:answer/id #uuid "179fe940-7b73-5546-bf32-fed03990fd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250762} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8d6af1-4d22-5cfb-b898-7e256d885ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250789} {:answer/id #uuid "3475e5a6-689a-521d-b598-8eb44369e318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250988} {:answer/id #uuid "6287be61-1f4d-505f-b9e8-81ea18208894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179fe940-7b73-5546-bf32-fed03990fd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250762} :answer-field/id #uuid "154c7544-e9aa-5942-a1f1-f550a4df2949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7483895f-9f2e-5510-9cf9-357e34d2424a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119381" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ed664b-fff1-5712-ac2e-5525f9cdacef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250634} {:answer/id #uuid "3b69e247-6d23-5ff1-a976-eb6503b80dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251045} {:answer/id #uuid "58c39cbe-5a9b-575c-ae8a-d7f92d34e4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251282} {:answer/id #uuid "923c3e09-f2e0-5124-82ce-83280737e8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251804} {:answer/id #uuid "b061ebd1-c842-5f84-80fa-eec468f6b43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ed664b-fff1-5712-ac2e-5525f9cdacef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250634} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a2bbe3-2ba2-5a56-9f75-7bcd2efd08bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e604df29-4056-5a18-af72-ee9756feedd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-119387" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "103f5b2e-5c31-5097-a363-9f6afaafdbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250694} {:answer/id #uuid "4b13d84e-fa74-5321-92fd-9d3ab8999d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251178} {:answer/id #uuid "53ddef33-f78b-53ce-9fde-d6f939e3fb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251239} {:answer/id #uuid "a784c34d-c4aa-591d-a102-942798280f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251996} {:answer/id #uuid "da6b22ed-a42d-50cf-92ea-c1fdfd820128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53ddef33-f78b-53ce-9fde-d6f939e3fb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251239} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15dbfd9-4666-5a0a-a3af-8408df3d5a73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c41ec619-a5e7-5d9c-af90-cb7a886021e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119392" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5849bb-789c-55dc-b22f-663e67e3571e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251441} {:answer/id #uuid "a278e6d5-4579-5dbc-89f7-1919dc0a81a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251954} {:answer/id #uuid "c069559c-6260-51c1-a64b-9bed21216b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252252} {:answer/id #uuid "c802eca5-1c87-5dfc-ae16-0c9da3679cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252326} {:answer/id #uuid "f758c764-6980-50ac-860d-7a0a1279d166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f758c764-6980-50ac-860d-7a0a1279d166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252715} :answer-field/id #uuid "862ad186-b2f1-59fa-b8f3-cd1202dce3d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d3dca9-aff5-5370-bb54-448ec1d2e38e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119764" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the first term using the definition of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d921589-04fa-57cf-b244-978da47124ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250802} {:answer/id #uuid "981af32a-b543-562f-a722-27d17840b262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251860} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a7046c-f34f-5960-95ca-1c2d73520766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251939} {:answer/id #uuid "a8221673-73e3-5e15-b330-5c44df97503f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252005} {:answer/id #uuid "ad78031b-233e-5a8e-a9e2-0d0f1f88049e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d921589-04fa-57cf-b244-978da47124ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250802} :answer-field/id #uuid "31a95a2f-0045-5d71-b0d3-ea8658460213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a82c56b9-720e-52fc-8dc1-2a735f11a49c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119767" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55eb6103-d65c-564e-8146-1b697fcf6114" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251257} {:answer/id #uuid "9c494cc4-f14a-523f-afab-b55ead4e2206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251902} {:answer/id #uuid "9cabf4a9-d334-52aa-94a3-29c1226a338c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251905} {:answer/id #uuid "ac59de0c-94ce-555a-a9af-0f345fa9844c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252052} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfac5b4-b918-541c-bab0-02afa81cd836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac59de0c-94ce-555a-a9af-0f345fa9844c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252052} :answer-field/id #uuid "5889b846-4b45-54d4-a4c7-1acb0782d3ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a4d16bb-7544-56af-8e64-b1dbb3f56d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119770" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=1.\n$$"}]}
